Nodephell package build for Linux Mint 22.3 / Ubuntu 24.04
==========================================================

This packaging is based on Ubuntu Noble's python3.12 source package
3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16. Ubuntu's complete Debian patch series remains intact and
the historical-package-store prototype is applied as its final quilt patch:

    debian/patches/nodephell-historical-store.patch

The local package version is:

    3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16+nodephell1

That version sorts after Ubuntu's 0.16 package but before a future 0.17
security update. This is intentional: the experiment must not silently block
new distro security updates.

Build
-----

Install the architecture-dependent build dependencies from the repository
root:

    sudo apt-get build-dep --arch-only .

Then build the architecture-dependent unsigned packages needed for the system
interpreter:

    dpkg-buildpackage --build=any --no-sign -jauto

The resulting .deb files are written to the parent directory. Building does
not install them or alter the running system Python.

Installation safety
-------------------

Install the matching packages together with apt, rather than copying files
into /usr or running upstream ``make install``. At minimum this normally
includes python3.12-minimal, libpython3.12-minimal, libpython3.12-stdlib, and
python3.12. Also include any locally installed matching packages such as
libpython3.12t64, python3.12-dev, libpython3.12-dev, and python3.12-venv.

Keep a bootable Mint live USB and the official Ubuntu packages available for
recovery. Do not remove the EXTERNALLY-MANAGED marker. The historical store is
additive and does not require ordinary pip to modify distro-managed paths.

Before installation, record the current package state:

    dpkg-query -W 'python3.12*' 'libpython3.12*'

After installation, verify Python, APT, and the historical importer before
rebooting. An optional apt hold can keep the experiment in place, but it also
blocks security upgrades and must be reviewed whenever Ubuntu publishes a new
python3.12 revision.
